WEBVTT

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.320
Shall we race?

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:13.280
M-Midousuji? Kyoto Fushimi's ace?

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:20.060
Since it's a 600-meter track, how does 
a ten-lap, six-kilometer race sound?

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.860
Sure. It's my last race.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.120
Give me everything you've got.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:29.920
But it wouldn't be fun to just race.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.280
Why don't we each bet something important?

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.430
That's Naruko, the sprinter from
 national champion Sohoku,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.140
and Kyoto Fushimi's first-year ace Midousuji!

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.100
And they're about to have a sprint showdown?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.070
Seriously? I can't believe we 
get to watch that race here!

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.930
If I win the next race,
I'll keep riding as a sprinter.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.610
If I lose...

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.070
I'll quit sprinting!

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.470
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:38.220
You'll quit sprinting?

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:39.530
<i>RIDE.06  Naruko VS Midousuji</i>

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.590
You, the sprinter?

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.520
Yeah, what do you think?

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.350
This race just got really 
interesting, didn't it?

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.100
Gross!

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.210
<i>He's serious. This guy must be an idiot.</i>

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.110
<i>He actually bet something important to him.</i>

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:01.860
<i>But such purity can only 
be found in serious races.</i>

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.870
Gross, gross!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:09.000
<i>Fine. My heart hasn't beat 
this hard in a while.</i>

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.330
<i>This is exactly the kind of 
competition I was looking for.</i>

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.550
Mizuta-kun, Yamaguchi-kun...

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:27.680
If I lose this race, the five of you 
can ride in next year's Inter-High.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:34.060
I'll put on a yellow jersey and 
do everything I can to help

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.940
reigning champions Sohoku for three days.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.240
<b>Sohoku High
Bicycle Racing Club</b>

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.700
Yes, sir.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.330
<i>He's serious.</i>

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:57.100
Of course, if that ever happened, my head 
would split in two. I couldn't do it.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.720
So I have to win here.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:06.410
I heard you were lying in the first aid 
tent at the Inter-High for a long time.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.430
Did all that sleep leave you out of shape?

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.040
I was just resting.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.690
I can't do anything if the vessel 
carrying my soul is a wreck.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:22.050
Thanks to that, I recovered. 
Gradually, I recovered.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.950
Now, I'm even more flawless than before.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.490
They're coming around the turn!

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.870
They're passing under the fire hydrant sign!

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:32.160
Their ten-lap sprint...

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.660
...is starting!

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.580
Kyoto Fushimi's accelerating!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.310
How can he lean so far forward while dancing?

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.180
He's so fast!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.830
<i>Midousuji!</i>

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.060
But there's a turn coming up!

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:57.150
If he goes that fast into 
the turn, he'll fall!

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.680
<i>He won't fall.</i>

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:03.020
<i>He rounds corners with 
full-throttle dive banks!</i>

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.240
How can he turn at that speed?

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.040
Sohoku's falling behind!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.790
<i>He's fast. He's first-rate.</i>

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.790
<i>But I'm falling behind? Are they joking?</i>

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.990
They can't be serious!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.380
You going somewhere?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.210
You seem to be in a hurry.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.260
Are you holding back a poop?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:33.650
Sohoku sprinter, are you 
talking about yourself?

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.640
You're pedaling as fast as you can.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:37.390
Whoa!

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:41.480
What? They finished two laps 
in the time I finished one!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.530
Show me what you've really got!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.030
No, you.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.430
They're so fast.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.090
What's wrong with them?

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:52.180
Was Naruko holding back when he raced us?

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.040
They're both pushing each other forward.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.190
What?

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:58.370
Both their ability and competitive spirit.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.610
Kyoto Fushimi third-year...

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.130
...Ishigaki!

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>Will you make your next breakthrough in 
this race against Naruko-kun, Midousuji?</i>

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.350
<i>That's right.</i>

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.310
<i>This is exactly the kind of 
competition I was looking for.</i>

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.480
Sohoku's pulling ahead!

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.610
You're too slow, Turtle-suji.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.450
That's not something you should 
say when you're drenched in sweat,

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.940
you chicken-headed bean!

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.740
Fall!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.880
Shut up!

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:35.810
Fall!

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.500
No, you fall!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.330
Fall!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.000
Idiot!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.580
Second lap!

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.740
Third lap!

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.350
Fall!

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.220
I'm not falling, seaweed!

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.480
They're running into each other...

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.980
As they pass us!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.730
Fourth lap!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.460
You want to keep going?

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:07.320
This race is about to become 
so back-breakingly intense,

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.900
you'll wish you'd dropped out now.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.880
Thanks. That's exactly what I'm looking for.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.660
Make it as hard as you can.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.840
You must be stupid.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:17.990
Why'd you scream about seaweed?

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:19.040
That's you.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.790
You're long and drift around everywhere!

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.420
They're changing positions 
as they ride with dizzying speed!

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.670
They've gotten even faster on this lap!

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:31.560
Will this race be a draw?

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.990
Seaweed!

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.290
<i>Watching him ride from behind 
sends chills down my spine.</i>

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.310
<i>All my hair's standing on end.</i>

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:47.730
<i>He's different from everyone 
else I've ridden against.</i>

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:50.990
<i>He has no doubts. He's decisive.</i>

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:58.160
<i>It's like he's carving away everything 
unnecessary with a knife or something.</i>

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.290
<i>He only rides to move forward!</i>

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:06.170
<i>His style has changed!</i>

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.460
Seaweed!

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.880
<i>He's stronger than he was at the Inter-High!</i>

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.260
Fifth lap!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.390
You've been speaking less.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:28.330
After becoming the champions of the 
Inter-High and hugging each other,

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.510
praising each other, 
congratulating each other,

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:34.150
and discussing how important 
your friends are...

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.830
Are you sure you didn't forget to practice?

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:45.250
You're right. I may have forgotten.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.940
Sohoku's Naruko pulled 
ahead of him in the turn!

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:54.720
He's trying to keep Kyoto Fushimi in check!

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.300
Keep you in check? I wouldn't do that.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.390
I'm the Sprinter of Naniwa!

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.390
I always aim to be flashy!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.730
Playtime is over!

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.900
I'm pulling ahead!

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.500
Sixth lap!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.120
<i>He jumped ahead. Was that 
not as fast as he could go?</i>

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.670
<i>That acceleration's the real thing.</i>

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:21.220
<i>This technique, this heartbeat, 
this wariness, this pressure.</i>

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:26.080
<i>He's no ordinary chicken-head!</i>

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.210
Kyoto Fushimi's falling behind!

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.960
<i>So he's been observing me until now?</i>

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.970
<i>Me? Observing me?</i>

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.220
<i>He's been appraising me?</i>

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:45.480
<i>And he jumped ahead because 
he thought he could win?</i>

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:47.020
<i>I can win.</i>

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.460
<i>You were right. I did forget to practice.</i>

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:55.070
<i>After all, our team had a bear with 
a giant attitude and body on it.</i>

00:09:55.070 --> 00:10:00.550
<i>Because I was anxious to beat him, 
I didn't have a chance to rest!</i>

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:05.250
<i>And partway through, a super-fast 
but silent mole popped up, too.</i>

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.500
Unfortunately for you, Midousuji, 
since the Inter-High,

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:14.250
I've gotten stronger not during practice,
but during actual races!

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.970
<i>Sorry. That told me everything 
I needed to know.</i>

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.510
<i>I'm the faster sprinter.</i>

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:27.170
<i>I'll show you just how fast 
the genius Naruko can sprint!</i>

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.710
He's so fast!

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:36.190
Sohoku's been riding exceptionally 
fast since he jumped ahead!

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:41.980
This is how fast the genius Naruko sprints!

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.250
They're starting their seventh lap.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.520
There's four laps to go.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.410
Kyoto Fushimi's falling behind.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:57.510
If Midousuji-kun loses, only five of 
us will ride at next year's Inter-High.

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:02.080
Anything goes in an unofficial race.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.010
No one said it had to be one-on-one.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.810
I'm going to go help Midousuji-kun.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.020
You don't need to go, Nobu.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:16.380
Are you sure it's okay for you 
to call me Nobu, Ishigaki-san?

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:20.570
Midousuji-kun told us to call each 
other by our numbers or use honorifics.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.110
It's fine. I retired from the club.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.950
I'll call you whatever I want, Nobuyuki.

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:31.540
What do you mean, we don't 
have to go help him?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.380
He's been waiting for this moment.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:43.270
For someone as physically and mentally 
strong as he is to accept his challenge.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:49.730
He's become too strong. No one 
can challenge him anymore.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:54.150
Since the Inter-High ended, 
his riding style has changed.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:57.360
Really? It looks the same to me.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:04.870
No, he's started carefully considering 
and treating each practice and each race.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.850
He's always been that way, 
but it's like he's honed it.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:10.370
Like he's searching for something.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:15.880
It seemed to me like he was waiting for 
something to break him out of his shell.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:20.880
He's the one in control of this race.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:26.130
Just as an insect breaks through its 
exoskeleton to become stronger and larger,

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:32.210
he's trying to shed his skin, too.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:38.430
<i>I wanted competition.</i>

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.220
<i>Win or lose... I can't lose.</i>

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.110
<i>Something important.</i>

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:59.190
<i>Something that's only born
from this kind of intensity.</i>

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.300
<i>This is the shock I was looking for.</i>

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.830
<i>It's time to fly.</i>

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:15.820
<i>Just as insects metamorphose and 
take flight in search of life</i>

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.150
<i>when an area becomes overpopulated...</i>

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.650
<i>To achieve my next victory...</i>

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.320
<i>I will fly, too!</i>

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:34.410
A battle cry? Midousuji-kun!

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:38.750
<i>Midousuji, is this your next form?</i>

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.140
Eighth lap!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.640
What the hell is that?

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.960
He stretched his back straight forward!

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.060
His form is so strange, but...

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.110
He's fast!

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:04.480
He's trying to catch up with 
less than 1.8 kilometers to go.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.240
But he's almost half a lap behind.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.530
Can he do that?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.000
<i>Midousuji...</i>

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:18.710
<b>Kyoto
Fushimi
High</b>

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.460
<b>Bicycle
Racing
Club</b>

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.650
Good work.

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.230
It's no good.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.590
What's wrong, Midousuji?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:31.470
I know your time wasn't 
good today, but it happens.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:35.740
You rode incredibly at 
this year's Inter-High.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.810
You're the pride of the team.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.650
You don't need to be so hard on yourself.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:44.910
It's not a physical burden.

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.610
I can't move onto the next stage like this.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.990
It's something different.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.490
Something mental, as well.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.750
Something back-breaking...

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.920
You've been wearing those while you practice?

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:01.860
Midousuji...

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.150
A race...

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:07.130
<i>He can't hear me.</i>

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:15.140
Living creatures only evolve under 
truly difficult circumstances.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:19.140
<i>It's fine. Don't look back.</i>

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:26.110
<i>Keep chasing after the new form you see.</i>

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.910
<i>He's getting closer.</i>

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.910
Two laps left!

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.670
Sohoku's riding ahead!

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:38.910
He's going to make it!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.210
<i>It's not my imagination.</i>

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:44.990
<i>He's coming.</i>

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:47.410
Interesting.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:50.300
I'm impressed, Midousuji.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.430
You still had that much potential left?

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:58.060
But I won't let you catch up!

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.890
<i>What is he doing?</i>

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:07.750
<i>He's different. I can feel it.</i>

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.110
<i>My fingers are shaking.</i>

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:12.530
<i>What kind of ridiculous pressure is this?</i>

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.870
<i>Hey, wait! I'm not letting you catch me!</i>

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.060
<i>I'm the fastest, flashiest man on the track!</i>

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:21.280
<i>The Speedman of Naniwa, Naruko Shoukichi!</i>

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.580
No way!

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:29.170
<i>What kind of crazy form is that? 
I've never seen anything like it.</i>

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.970
<i>Has he been...</i>

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:38.890
Oh, you're behind me now, bean?

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.090
I'm facing downwards, so I didn't notice.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:50.320
That's not good. I can't go 
fast unless I face forward.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:52.150
One more lap!

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.110
Kyoto Fushimi's ahead of Sohoku!

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.480
You seem desperate, bean.

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:02.580
But I can see it.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:07.580
I can see myself raising my hands in victory!

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:09.530
<i>Crap!</i>

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:11.880
My nose is bleeding.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.880
Naruko...

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:18.010
Honestly, I want Naruko to win.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:21.640
The way he stretched for the 
finish line was the real deal.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.750
Me, too. He's a pure sprinter.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:28.050
And the third time's the charm.

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.610
Naruko, you can do it!

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:42.370
<i>What is this? I was supposed 
to pull ahead and win.</i>

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:43.870
<i>But he caught up.</i>

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.870
<i>He caught up and passed me.</i>

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.710
<i>Why is Idiot-suji riding so far ahead of me?</i>

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:54.110
<i>I'm the one who knows this track!</i>

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:56.880
<i>I'm the genius sprinter of Naniwa!</i>

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:58.380
<i>I...</i>

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.890
...always win, no matter the circumstances!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.810
<i>Road races are make-or-break!</i>

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.570
<i>You only get one shot!</i>

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:16.260
<i>The are two possible results: win or lose.</i>

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:20.290
<i>I'll give everything I've got 
and put my life on the line!</i>

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:23.990
<i>I'll bet everything and put it all out there!</i>

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:26.230
Win or lose...

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.170
That's why I'm on fire!

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:31.670
He caught up on the straight!

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.460
<i>He's fast. We're going so fast,
my nose is bleeding.</i>

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:38.170
<i>Honestly, my heart and muscles are screaming.</i>

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:42.180
<i>He's evolved during this race.</i>

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.510
<i>Right here. Unbelievably!</i>

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:48.730
<i>But so what? I'll win!</i>

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.060
<i>I'll do everything I can and win!</i>

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.230
He threw away his water bottle!

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.730
He's making himself lighter for the sprint!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.990
He zipped up his jersey to 
reduce his wind resistance!

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:06.700
He even threw away his saddle!

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.080
I will win!

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.390
He's made himself as light as possible!

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:11.920
I don't believe it.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.790
He's determined to win.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.890
I'm Naruko Shoukichi!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.220
They're entering the last turn!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.720
When will I go, if not now?

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:26.600
One hundred and twenty meters left!

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:30.100
If I lose, I'll quit sprinting.

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:34.820
I can't quit! Sprinting is my way of life!

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.020
My pride!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.370
Bean, bean...

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.490
You're not a bean.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.320
You're a chicken-headed turtle.

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.710
I did it.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.910
If I lost here, no matter 
how cutting-edge the change,

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:03.640
it couldn't be called an evolution.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:07.310
But I won. I am victorious.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.220
I did it.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:12.980
I achieved my next form.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:22.080
<i>In my hometown of Osaka, 
on a track I've ridden to death,</i>

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:29.210
<i>I gave everything I had until 
my nose bled, and I lost.</i>

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.250
Damn it!

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.980
I'm always the loser!

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:39.250
Idiot! Moron! I wish I could die!

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:40.580
Naruko...

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:41.510
Don't.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:46.180
Aren't you going to quit, sprinter?

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:49.780
That's what you said before we started.

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:52.660
Yeah, I'll quit.

00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:55.730
A man never goes back on his word.

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:05.520
Sohoku has lost one of its feathers.

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:08.330
And they just became champions, too.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:14.500
Naruko-kun might come back to race again.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.250
What? What does that mean?

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:19.500
Midousuji...

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:24.380
Frustration makes people stronger.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:21.460
<b>Ishigaki Koutarou (9 Years Old)</b>

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:23.190
There it is.

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:27.190
Patience, patience.

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:30.470
Gross!

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:35.210
Was that you?

00:23:35.210 --> 00:23:36.220
What?

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT RIDE  The Last Meet</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
